Usage: cpio [OPTION]

Copy files to and from archives.
Copy files to and from cpio archives. Supports creating, extracting,
and listing archive contents. Uses new ASCII format (070701/070702).

OPTIONS:
  -o, --create                      create archive
  -i, --extract                     extract archive
  -t, --list                        list archive contents
  -p, --pass-through                run in copy-pass mode
  -d, --make-directories            create leading directories where needed
  -m, --preserve-modification-time  preserve modification time
  -v, --verbose                     verbose output
  -H, --format ARG                  use given archive FORMAT
  -R, --owner ARG                   set the ownership of all files
      --help                        display this help and exit
  -V, --version                     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
